# /etc/onionwarden/wildcard-listener.allow — explicit exceptions to the
# "no process may listen on a wildcard address" rule (lib/checks/wildcard_listener.sh).
#
# Format: one exception per line, exactly  <comm>:<port>:<proto>
#   - all three fields must match exactly (proto specificity matters)
#   - lines starting with '#' are comments; a '#' later on a line is inline
#   - blank lines and malformed lines are ignored
#
# The shipped default is EMPTY: nothing is permitted until you add it. Every
# entry MUST carry a SECURITY justification — a wildcard bind exposes the
# service on every network this host is attached to.
#
# Examples (commented out — uncomment only what YOU intend to expose):
#
# SECURITY: management SSH reachable fleet-wide by policy (reviewed 2026-06-06, jdoe).
#sshd:22:tcp
#
# SECURITY: <who reviewed, why it must be wildcard, when>
#<comm>:<port>:<proto>
